      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The claim that a specific plan will cause a \"total economic collapse\" is a strong and often partisan claim that is not definitively supported by all economic analysis.\n\nMost comprehensive economic impact studies would likely point to a complex range of potential effects, such as changes in the labor force, but \"total collapse\" is an extreme outcome that is hard to substantiate with facts in this context.\n\nThe actual impact would depend heavily on the specific policy details, the level of enforcement, and the strength of the US and global and related economic systems.\n\nFor a balanced view, I would recommend looking for independent, non-partisan analysis from think tanks that offer pro and con arguments for the policy, rather than focusing solely on one op-ed.",
