      "role": "user",
      "content": "But that's exactly my point. If the risks are that \"severe\" and \"primary,\" then how can anyone argue this is a sustainable policy? It feels like people supporting this are just ignoring the fundamental math of the economy just to make a political point. Isn't it basically irresponsible to propose something that has a high probability of causing a recession?",
